y  important that this organization is not  used  as a tool in the political game of  what's happening right now  well a number of russian forces in  belarus is the largest since the end of  the cold war they're engaged in  intensive war games that nato considers  a potential prelude to an invasion al  jazeera's step faster reports now from  an airfield near the border with ukraine  at the sabrevika airfield russian  helicopter gunships take to the air  nearby dozens of russian trucks leave  the training grounds  armoured personnel carriers are  transported towards the border with  ukraine the south of belarus looks like  a russian military zone  this abandoned airfield in sabrovka near  the city of hommel is one of the 12  areas where russia and belarus are  conducting joint drills known as allied  resolve  visitors are not allowed in but local  people tell us the airstrip is in bad  shape and has recently been used for  sports competitions  footage released by the russian ministry  of defense shows state-of-the-art  military equipment in action near the  border between belarus and ukraine and  nato  several divisions of s-400 missile  defense systems and dozens of sukhoi  fighter jets are taking part in the  exercises  in response to questions from the baltic  states belarus has confirmed that  russian forces are also active outside  the scope of these drills  some military units and subunits from  the eastern military district of the  armed forces of the russian federation  are performing tasks outside the  framework of the exercise  they have been deployed and are  performing practical measures to guard a  southern state border where there are no  opportunities to reinforce it using  border patrol units of the republic of  belarus there are a lot of questions  about the exact size and the real  purpose of these exercises happening  around 20 kilometers from the border  with ukraine for sure russian forces are  a lot more active this close to the  ukrainian capit